IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssa-common`
IMPORT `ssa-figures`
IMPORT `ssa-title-ii`
IMPORT `ssa-title-xvi`
IMPORT `ssa-medicare`

-- Social Security Act -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom the Act is applied -- the worker earning credits, the retiree, the survivor of a worker who
-- has died, the disabled person, the SSI applicant, and the person reaching Medicare age. One person, asking about their own
-- record. Every question here calls the rules in ssa-title-ii.l4, ssa-title-xvi.l4 and ssa-medicare.l4 and the dated table
-- in ssa-figures.l4; nothing here is new law. Inputs are plain facts the person can state, with a month given as a year and a
-- month number (1-12). Judgments the Act leaves to the Commissioner (disability, blindness, dependency) are asked as facts:
-- the answer then holds "if the Commissioner so finds".
--
-- The groups follow the Act: the worker (Title II credits), the retiree, the working beneficiary, the survivor (situation:
-- someone on whose record I may claim has died), the disabled person (situation: I cannot work because of an impairment),
-- the SSI applicant (situation: I am 65 or over, blind or disabled, with little income and few resources), Medicare, and
-- appeals (situation: I have a decision I disagree with).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Social Security Act -- questions for the individual`

§§ `The worker -- quarters of coverage and insured status`

@export How many quarters of coverage (Social Security credits) do my earnings in a year give me? (s 413(a)(2), (d); 2026 figures only)
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the earnings were paid in, e.g. 2026 (only 2026 is covered)
      `my earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total wages and net self-employment income for that year, in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How many quarters of coverage do my earnings give me` MEANS
    `the quarters of coverage credited for the year` `calendar year` `my earnings`

@export Am I "fully insured" for Social Security retirement and survivor benefits under s 414(a), judged at the year I reach 62?
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601, e.g. 1964-05-10
      `my quarters of coverage` IS A NUMBER @desc The total number of quarters of coverage (credits) on your earnings record
      `years in a period of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar years after you turned 21 were partly in a period of disability you had under Social Security (usually 0)
      `I am a US citizen or national, or have a work-authorised Social Security number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a US citizen or national, or your Social Security number was assigned for work (or you worked on a B or D visa within its terms), as s 414(c) requires
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I fully insured for retirement` IF
    `is a fully insured individual` `my quarters of coverage`
        (`the elapsed years for fully insured status` `my birth date` (`the year in which age is attained` `my birth date` 62) `years in a period of disability`)
        `I am a US citizen or national, or have a work-authorised Social Security number`

@export Am I insured for Social Security disability insurance benefits in a given month? (s 423(c)(1))
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `year asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the month you ask about, usually the month your disability began
      `month asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1-12) you ask about
      `my quarters of coverage` IS A NUMBER @desc The total number of quarters of coverage on your record up to that month
      `quarters of coverage in the last 40 quarters` IS A NUMBER @desc Quarters of coverage in the 40 quarters (10 years) ending with the quarter of that month
      `quarters of coverage since I turned 21` IS A NUMBER @desc Quarters of coverage in the quarters after the one in which you turned 21, up to and including the quarter of that month
      `quarters of coverage in the last 12 quarters` IS A NUMBER @desc Quarters of coverage in the 12 quarters ending with the quarter of that month
      `years in a period of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar years after you turned 21 were partly in an earlier period of disability (usually 0)
      `I am blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are blind: central visual acuity of 20/200 or less in the better eye with correcting lens, or a visual field of 20 degrees or less (s 416(i)(1))
      `I am a US citizen or national, or have a work-authorised Social Security number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a US citizen or national, or meet the Social Security number or visa criterion of s 414(c)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I insured for disability benefits in the month` IF
    `is insured for disability insurance benefits in the month` `my birth date` m
        (`is a fully insured individual` `my quarters of coverage` (`the elapsed years for fully insured status` `my birth date` (`the year of month number` m) `years in a period of disability`) `I am a US citizen or national, or have a work-authorised Social Security number`)
        `quarters of coverage in the last 40 quarters` `quarters of coverage since I turned 21` `quarters of coverage in the last 12 quarters` `I am blind`
    WHERE m MEANS `the month number of` `year asked about` `month asked about`

§§ `The retiree -- retirement age, the PIA and the old-age benefit`

@export In which month do I reach full retirement age ("retirement age", s 416(l)) for my own retirement benefit?
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601, e.g. 1960-05-10
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`When do I reach full retirement age` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the month retirement age is attained for an old-age benefit` `my birth date`)

@export What is my primary insurance amount (PIA), the full-retirement-age benefit, if I reach 62 in 2026? (s 415(a)(1), 2026 bend points)
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601; the bend points used are those for the year you reach 62
      `my average indexed monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average indexed monthly earnings (AIME) in US dollars, from your Social Security statement or computation
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my primary insurance amount` MEANS
    `the primary insurance amount for the year of eligibility` (`the year in which age is attained` `my birth date` 62) `my average indexed monthly earnings`

@export If I apply for my retirement benefit in a given month, from which month can it begin? (s 402(a), (j)(1), (j)(4))
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `year I apply` IS A NUMBER @desc The year in which you file your application
      `month I apply` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1-12) in which you file your application
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`From which month can my retirement benefit begin` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the first month of old-age benefits on an application` `my birth date` (`the month number of` `year I apply` `month I apply`))

@export How much is my monthly retirement (old-age) benefit if it starts in a given month, with the reduction for starting early or the increase for starting late? (s 402(a), (q), (w), s 415(g))
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `I am fully insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are fully insured (normally 40 quarters of coverage); see the fully insured question
      `my primary insurance amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your primary insurance amount (PIA) for the month, in US dollars, after any cost-of-living increases
      `year benefits start` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the first month of your retirement benefit
      `month benefits start` IS A NUMBER @desc The first month (1-12) of your retirement benefit
      `months my benefits were withheld for work before full retirement age` IS A NUMBER @desc For the amount from full retirement age on: the months before it in which your whole benefit was withheld because of your earnings (0 for the amount when payments begin)
GIVETH A `Benefit answer`
`How much is my retirement benefit` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am fully insured`
        THEN `no benefit` "not fully insured (s 402(a)(1), s 414(a))"
        ELSE IF start LESS THAN `the first month throughout which the age is attained` `my birth date` 62
            THEN `no benefit` "not yet 62 throughout the month (s 402(a)(2), (B))"
            ELSE `a monthly benefit of` (`the old-age insurance benefit` `my birth date` `my primary insurance amount` start `months my benefits were withheld for work before full retirement age`)
    WHERE start MEANS `the month number of` `year benefits start` `month benefits start`

@export What is the most that can be paid each month to me and my family on my record (the family maximum), if I reach 62 in 2026? (s 403(a)(1))
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `my primary insurance amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your primary insurance amount (PIA), in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my family maximum` MEANS
    `the family maximum for the year of eligibility` (`the year in which age is attained` `my birth date` 62) `my primary insurance amount`

§§ `The working beneficiary -- the earnings test and the report of earnings`

-- Situation: I get Social Security benefits and I also work, before full retirement age.

@export How much of my Social Security benefits for a year will be withheld because of my earnings? (the retirement earnings test, s 403(b), (f); 2026 exempt amounts)
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year, e.g. 2026 (only 2026 is covered)
      `where I am in the year` IS AN `Earnings test year` @desc One of: under retirement age for the whole year; the year retirement age is attained; retirement age attained before the year began
      `my earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your wages plus net self-employment earnings for the year, in US dollars; in the year you reach full retirement age, only those before the month you reach it
      `monthly benefits on my record` IS A NUMBER @desc The monthly benefits paid on your record, yours plus any family members', in US dollars
      `months that can be charged` IS A NUMBER @desc The months of the year you are entitled to benefits and below full retirement age, less any month in your first year of benefits in which you did not work over the monthly exempt amount
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much of my benefits will be withheld for my earnings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the excess earnings for the year` `calendar year` `where I am in the year` `my earnings`
    WHEN `answered` x THEN `answered` (`the deductions on account of work` x `monthly benefits on my record` `months that can be charged`)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r

@export Must I report my earnings for the year to the Social Security Administration? (s 403(h)(1)(A))
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year, e.g. 2026 (only 2026 is covered)
      `I was entitled to benefits during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to a monthly Social Security benefit for any month of the year
      `where I am in the year` IS AN `Earnings test year` @desc One of: under retirement age for the whole year; the year retirement age is attained; retirement age attained before the year began
      `my earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your wages plus net self-employment earnings for the year, in US dollars
      `all my benefits were suspended for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Social Security suspended all your benefits for the months below full retirement age under s 403(h)(3), with no family member in another household affected
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`Must I report my earnings for the year` MEANS
    `a report of earnings is required` `calendar year` `I was entitled to benefits during the year` `where I am in the year` `my earnings` `all my benefits were suspended for the year`

@export By what date must I report my earnings for a year to the Social Security Administration? (s 403(h)(1)(A))
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year the earnings were for
      `months of extension granted` IS A NUMBER @desc Months of extension the Commissioner has granted you (0 to 4)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I report my earnings` MEANS
    `the last day for the report of earnings` `calendar year` `months of extension granted`

@export If I do not report my earnings on time, how much more will be deducted from my benefits? (s 403(h)(2), (l))
GIVEN `which failure this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first failure to report on time, 2 for the second, 3 or more after that
      `my benefit for the last month of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your benefit for the last month of the year in which you were entitled, in US dollars
      `the deduction for my earnings that year` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount deducted for the year under the earnings test, in US dollars
      `I had good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Social Security accepts you had good cause, taking account of any physical, mental, educational or language limitation (s 403(l))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much more is deducted for not reporting my earnings` MEANS
    `the additional deduction for a failure to report earnings` `which failure this is` `my benefit for the last month of the year` `the deduction for my earnings that year` `I had good cause`

§§ `The survivor -- widow's, widower's, child's and lump-sum benefits`

-- Situation: a worker on whose record I may claim (my spouse, former spouse or parent) has died.

@export Am I the "widow", "widower" or "surviving divorced spouse" of the worker who died, for Social Security survivor benefits? (s 416(c), (d), (g), (k))
GIVEN `my relationship to the worker` IS A `Survivor relationship` @desc One of: married to the deceased at the death; divorced from the deceased; neither
      `months we were married before the death` IS A NUMBER @desc If married at the death: how many months you had been married immediately before the death
      `I am the parent of the worker's child, or another s 416(c) ground applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the parent of the worker's son or daughter, adopted a child with or of the worker while married, or were entitled to certain Social Security benefits in the month before the marriage
      `the nine-month rule is waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death was accidental or in line of military duty, or you had been married to the worker before (s 416(k))
      `years we were married before the divorce` IS A NUMBER @desc If divorced: how many years you had been married immediately before the divorce became effective
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I the widow, widower or surviving divorced spouse` IF
    `is the widow or widower, or surviving divorced spouse` `my relationship to the worker` `months we were married before the death` `I am the parent of the worker's child, or another s 416(c) ground applies` `the nine-month rule is waived` `years we were married before the divorce`

@export How much is my monthly widow's or widower's benefit from a given first month, if I am entitled? (s 402(e), (f), (q), s 415(g))
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `year benefits start` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the first month of your widow's or widower's benefit
      `month benefits start` IS A NUMBER @desc The first month (1-12) of your widow's or widower's benefit
      `the worker died fully insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker who died was fully insured (s 414(a))
      `I am the widow, widower or surviving divorced spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the worker's widow, widower or surviving divorced spouse (see that question)
      `I am not married, or married again only after 60` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now unmarried, or your present marriage took place after you were 60 (or after 50 while disabled)
      `Social Security finds I am under a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are 50 to 59: whether Social Security finds you under a disability (s 423(d)); otherwise FALSE
      `year of the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The year the worker died
      `month of the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1-12) the worker died
      `year my disability began` IS A NUMBER @desc If disabled: the year your disability began (otherwise any year)
      `month my disability began` IS A NUMBER @desc If disabled: the month (1-12) your disability began (otherwise any month)
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have filed an application for the widow's or widower's benefit
      `my own retirement benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own monthly retirement benefit, in US dollars (0 if none)
      `the worker's primary insurance amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The deceased worker's primary insurance amount (PIA), in US dollars
      `the worker's retirement benefit with delayed retirement credits` IS A NUMBER @desc If the worker started retirement benefits after full retirement age: that increased monthly benefit, in US dollars (otherwise 0)
      `the worker took a reduced early retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker received a retirement benefit reduced for starting before full retirement age
      `the worker's reduced benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: the reduced monthly benefit the worker would now be getting, in US dollars (otherwise 0)
GIVETH A `Benefit answer`
`How much is my widow's or widower's benefit` MEANS
    IF `is entitled to a widow's or widower's insurance benefit for the month` `my birth date` start `the worker died fully insured` `I am the widow, widower or surviving divorced spouse` `I am not married, or married again only after 60` `disabled in time` `I have applied` `my own retirement benefit` `the worker's primary insurance amount`
        THEN `a monthly benefit of` (`the widow's or widower's insurance benefit` `my birth date` start `the worker's primary insurance amount` `the worker's retirement benefit with delayed retirement credits` `the worker took a reduced early retirement benefit` `the worker's reduced benefit`)
        ELSE `no benefit` "not entitled to a widow's or widower's benefit for that month (s 402(e)(1), (f)(1))"
    WHERE
        start MEANS `the month number of` `year benefits start` `month benefits start`
        `disabled in time` MEANS
                `Social Security finds I am under a disability`
            AND `the disability began within the s 402(e)(4) period` `my birth date` (`the month number of` `year of the death` `month of the death`) (`the month number of` `year my disability began` `month my disability began`)

@export In which month does full retirement age for a widow's or widower's benefit fall for me? (s 416(l), early retirement age 60)
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`When do I reach full retirement age for a survivor benefit` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the month retirement age is attained for a widow's or widower's benefit` `my birth date`)

@export Is a child entitled to child's benefits on the record of a parent who has died, retired or become disabled, and how much (before the family maximum)? (s 402(d))
GIVEN `the parent is entitled to retirement or disability benefits, or died insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parent gets Social Security retirement or disability benefits, or died fully or currently insured
      `the parent has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parent has died
      `the child is the parent's child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is the parent's child, adopted child, or a qualifying stepchild or grandchild (s 416(e))
      `an application has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application for child's benefits has been filed for the child
      `the child was unmarried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was unmarried when the application was filed
      `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age when the application was filed
      `the child is a full-time school student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a full-time elementary or secondary school student
      `the child has a disability that began before 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Social Security finds the child under a disability that began before age 22
      `the child was dependent on the parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was dependent on the parent as s 402(d)(3)-(4) defines (a parent's own child usually is)
      `the parent's primary insurance amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The parent's primary insurance amount (PIA), in US dollars
GIVETH A `Benefit answer`
`How much is a child's benefit` MEANS
    IF `is entitled to a child's insurance benefit` `the parent is entitled to retirement or disability benefits, or died insured` `the child is the parent's child` `an application has been filed` `the child was unmarried` `the child's age` `the child is a full-time school student` `the child has a disability that began before 22` `the child was dependent on the parent`
        THEN `a monthly benefit of` (`the child's insurance benefit before the family maximum` `the parent has died` `the parent's primary insurance amount`)
        ELSE `no benefit` "not entitled to a child's benefit (s 402(d)(1))"

@export How much of the Social Security lump-sum death payment do I get? (s 402(i), at most $255)
GIVEN `the worker died fully or currently insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker who died was fully or currently insured
      `the worker's primary insurance amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The deceased worker's primary insurance amount (PIA), in US dollars
      `who I am` IS A `Lump-sum position` @desc One of: the widow or widower living in the same household; a widow or widower entitled to a widow's, widower's, mother's or father's benefit for the month of death; one of the children entitled to child's benefits for the month of death; none of these
      `there is a widow or widower who lived with the worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a widow or widower who was living in the same household as the worker at the death
      `there is a widow or widower entitled for the month of death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a widow or widower entitled (or who would be on applying) to a widow's, widower's, mother's or father's benefit for the month of death
      `number of children entitled` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children are entitled (or would be on applying) to child's benefits for the month of death
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of the lump-sum death payment do I get` MEANS
    `the share of the lump-sum death payment` `the worker died fully or currently insured` `the worker's primary insurance amount` `who I am` `there is a widow or widower who lived with the worker` `there is a widow or widower entitled for the month of death` `number of children entitled`

@export By what date must I apply for the lump-sum death payment? (s 402(i): within two years after the death)
GIVEN `date of death` IS A DATE @desc The date the worker died, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for the lump-sum death payment` MEANS
    `date of death` PLUS `the days to apply for the lump-sum death payment` `date of death`

§§ `The disabled person -- disability insurance benefits`

-- Situation: I cannot work because of a physical or mental impairment.

@export Am I entitled to Social Security disability insurance benefits? (s 423(a)(1); the disability itself is Social Security's finding)
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `year asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the month you ask about
      `month asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1-12) you ask about
      `I am insured for disability benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are insured for disability benefits in that month (see that question)
      `I am a US citizen or national, or have a work-authorised Social Security number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a US citizen or national, or meet the Social Security number or visa criterion of s 423(a)(1)(C)
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have filed an application for disability insurance benefits
      `Social Security finds I am under a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Social Security finds (or would find) that you cannot do any substantial gainful activity because of a medically determinable impairment expected to last 12 months or end in death (s 423(d))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to disability insurance benefits` IF
    `is entitled to disability insurance benefits` `I am insured for disability benefits`
        (`the month number of` `year asked about` `month asked about` AT LEAST `the month retirement age is attained for an old-age benefit` `my birth date`)
        `I am a US citizen or national, or have a work-authorised Social Security number` `I have applied` `Social Security finds I am under a disability`

@export If I am entitled to disability insurance benefits, from which month are they paid? (s 423(a)(1), (b), (c)(2): after a five-month waiting period, or at once with ALS)
GIVEN `date my disability began` IS A DATE @desc The date your disability began, ISO 8601
      `year I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc The year you filed your application
      `month I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1-12) you filed your application
      `I have ALS` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been medically determined to have amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS)
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`From which month are my disability benefits paid` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the first month of disability insurance benefits` `date my disability began` (`the month number of` `year I applied` `month I applied`) `I have ALS`)

@export What is my disability benefit (my PIA), if my five-month waiting period begins in 2026? (s 423(a)(2), s 415(a)(1))
GIVEN `year my waiting period begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the first month of your waiting period (only 2026 is covered)
      `my average indexed monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average indexed monthly earnings (AIME), in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my disability benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the primary insurance amount for the year of eligibility` `year my waiting period begins` `my average indexed monthly earnings`
    WHEN `answered` p THEN `answered` (`rounded down to a whole dollar` p)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r

@export Are my monthly earnings above the substantial gainful activity amount? (s 423(d)(4)(A); the non-blind amount is set by regulation)
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year, e.g. 2026 (only 2026 is covered)
      `I am blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are blind as s 416(i)(1) defines
      `my monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly earnings from work, in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`Are my earnings above the substantial gainful activity amount` MEANS
    `earnings are above the substantial gainful activity amount` `calendar year` `I am blind` `my monthly earnings`

§§ `The SSI applicant -- Supplemental Security Income`

-- Situation: I am 65 or over, blind or disabled, and have little income and few resources.

@export Am I an "aged, blind, or disabled individual" who can get SSI? (s 1382c(a)(1))
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I am blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Social Security finds you blind (central visual acuity of 20/200 or less in the better eye with correcting lens, or field of 20 degrees or less)
      `I am disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Social Security finds you disabled (s 1382c(a)(3)): for an adult, unable to do substantial gainful activity because of an impairment expected to last 12 months or end in death
      `I live in the US and am a citizen or lawful permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in the United States and are a citizen, a lawful permanent resident, or otherwise permanently residing under color of law (other federal law may limit SSI for some non-citizens)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an aged, blind, or disabled individual` IF
    `is an aged, blind, or disabled individual` `my age` `I am blind` `I am disabled` `I live in the US and am a citizen or lawful permanent resident`

@export What is my countable income for SSI for a month, after the exclusions? (s 1382a; 2026 figures)
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year (only 2026 is covered)
      `my earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your wages and net self-employment earnings for the month, in US dollars (with an eligible spouse: both of yours)
      `my unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc All other income for the month, in US dollars, including Social Security benefits, pensions and cash support, but not State or local need-based assistance
      `need-based income other than State aid` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that unearned income, how much is paid on the basis of need by someone other than a State or local government (for example a needs-based veterans' pension)
      `I am a student under 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 22 and regularly attending school, college, university or vocational training
      `student exclusion already used this year` IS A NUMBER @desc If a student: earned income already excluded as a student earlier this year, in US dollars
      `my work expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc If blind: your work expenses; if disabled: impairment-related work expenses Social Security accepts; otherwise 0
      `I am blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are blind
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my countable income for SSI` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures for` `calendar year`
    WHEN JUST f THEN `answered` (`the countable income` income f)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered` `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`
    WHERE
        income MEANS `Monthly income` WITH
            `earned income` IS `my earned income`
            `unearned income, including Social Security benefits` IS `my unearned income`
            `part of the unearned income paid on the basis of need, other than State or local assistance` IS `need-based income other than State aid`
            -- excluded whole by s 1382a(b)(6), so not asked; no rule reads this field for the total.
            `need-based assistance from a State or local government` IS 0
            `is a student under 22 regularly attending school` IS `I am a student under 22`
            `student earned income already excluded earlier this year` IS `student exclusion already used this year`
            `impairment-related or blind work expenses` IS `my work expenses`
            `is blind` IS `I am blind`

@export How much SSI can I get for a month? (s 1382(a), (b), (e)(1), s 1382a, s 1382b; 2026 federal benefit rate, without any State supplement)
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year (only 2026 is covered)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I am blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Social Security finds you blind
      `I am disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Social Security finds you disabled
      `I live in the US and am a citizen or lawful permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in the United States and are a citizen or lawful permanent resident (or otherwise permanently residing under color of law)
      `I have an eligible spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live with a spouse who is also aged, blind or disabled and eligible (then the couple rate and couple limits apply)
      `I live with an ineligible spouse or am a child living with a parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live with a spouse who is not eligible, or you are under 18 and live with a parent (their income is then deemed, which is not covered)
      `where I live` IS A `Living arrangement` @desc One of: in my own household; in another person's household, receiving support and maintenance in kind from that person; throughout the month in a medical treatment facility, with Medicaid paying for my care; throughout the month an inmate of a public institution
      `my earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages and net self-employment earnings for the month, in US dollars
      `my unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc All other income for the month, in US dollars, including Social Security benefits, but not State or local need-based assistance
      `need-based income other than State aid` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the unearned income, how much is paid on the basis of need by someone other than a State or local government
      `I am a student under 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 22 and regularly attending school or training
      `student exclusion already used this year` IS A NUMBER @desc If a student: earned income already excluded earlier this year
      `my work expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc If blind: work expenses; if disabled: impairment-related work expenses; otherwise 0
      `my resources other than my home` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of everything you own except your home: cash, bank accounts, investments, vehicles, other property, in US dollars
      `resources the law excludes` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, the value the law excludes: one automobile and household goods within Social Security's limits, burial spaces, property essential to self-support, EITC and child tax credit refunds in the 9 months after receipt, and the other s 1382b(a) items
GIVETH A `Benefit answer`
`How much SSI can I get` MEANS
    `the SSI benefit for the month` `calendar year`
        (`is an aged, blind, or disabled individual` `my age` `I am blind` `I am disabled` `I live in the US and am a citizen or lawful permanent resident`)
        `I have an eligible spouse` `I live with an ineligible spouse or am a child living with a parent` `where I live` income
        (`the countable resources` `my resources other than my home` `resources the law excludes`)
    WHERE
        income MEANS `Monthly income` WITH
            `earned income` IS `my earned income`
            `unearned income, including Social Security benefits` IS `my unearned income`
            `part of the unearned income paid on the basis of need, other than State or local assistance` IS `need-based income other than State aid`
            -- excluded whole by s 1382a(b)(6), so not asked; no rule reads this field for the total.
            `need-based assistance from a State or local government` IS 0
            `is a student under 22 regularly attending school` IS `I am a student under 22`
            `student earned income already excluded earlier this year` IS `student exclusion already used this year`
            `impairment-related or blind work expenses` IS `my work expenses`
            `is blind` IS `I am blind`

@export From which month does my SSI application take effect? (s 1382(c)(7))
GIVEN `date I filed` IS A DATE @desc The date you filed your SSI application, ISO 8601
      `date I became eligible` IS A DATE @desc The date you met all the conditions for SSI (if before you filed, give the filing date)
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`From which month does my SSI application take effect` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the first month of SSI on an application` `date I filed` `date I became eligible`)

@export How much will my SSI be reduced if I fail to report a change, or report it late? (s 1383(e)(2))
GIVEN `which failure this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first failure or delay, 2 for the second, 3 or more after that
      `I was without fault or had good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were without fault, or had good cause (for example, a change of employer where you authorised Social Security to see your payroll records)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my SSI reduced for a late report` MEANS
    `the reduction for a failure or delay in reporting` `which failure this is` `I was without fault or had good cause`

§§ `Medicare -- Part A and Part B`

@export Am I entitled to Medicare Part A (hospital insurance) at 65 without buying it? (s 426(a))
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `year asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the month you ask about
      `month asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1-12) you ask about
      `I get Social Security monthly benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to Social Security monthly benefits (retirement, spouse's or survivor's)
      `I could get them if I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would be entitled to those benefits on applying (for example you are fully insured, or the spouse or widow(er) of an insured worker)
      `I get a railroad retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a qualified railroad retirement beneficiary
      `I would qualify counting Medicare-covered government work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would qualify if your Medicare-qualified government employment counted as covered employment
      `I have applied for Part A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have filed an application for hospital insurance benefits
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to Part A at 65` IF
    `is entitled to hospital insurance benefits under s 426(a)`
        (`the month number of` `year asked about` `month asked about` AT LEAST `the month in which age is attained` `my birth date` 65)
        `I get Social Security monthly benefits` `I could get them if I applied` `I get a railroad retirement benefit` `I would qualify counting Medicare-covered government work` `I have applied for Part A`

@export From which month does Medicare Part A start for me on disability? (s 426(b), (h): the 25th month of disability benefits, or the first with ALS)
GIVEN `year disability benefits began` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of your first month of entitlement to disability insurance benefits (or disabled widow's, widower's or child's benefits)
      `month disability benefits began` IS A NUMBER @desc That first month (1-12)
      `I have ALS` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been medically determined to have amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS)
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`From which month does Part A start on disability` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the first month of hospital insurance on disability` (`the month number of` `year disability benefits began` `month disability benefits began`) `I have ALS`)

@export Can I buy Medicare Part A because I am not otherwise entitled to it? (s 1395i-2(a))
GIVEN `I am 65 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reached 65
      `I am enrolled in Part B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled in Medicare Part B
      `I am a resident citizen, or a permanent resident here 5 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in the US and are a citizen, or a lawful permanent resident who has lived in the US continuously for the last 5 years
      `I am otherwise entitled to Part A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are already entitled to Part A without paying for it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I buy Part A` IF
    `may enroll in Part A under s 1395i-2` `I am 65 or over` `I am enrolled in Part B` `I am a resident citizen, or a permanent resident here 5 years` `I am otherwise entitled to Part A`

@export Am I eligible to enroll in Medicare Part B? (s 1395o(a))
GIVEN `I am entitled to Part A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to Medicare Part A
      `I am 65 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reached 65
      `I am a resident citizen, or a permanent resident here 5 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in the US and are a citizen, or a lawful permanent resident who has lived in the US continuously for the last 5 years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible to enroll in Part B` IF
    `is eligible to enroll in Part B` `I am entitled to Part A` `I am 65 or over` `I am a resident citizen, or a permanent resident here 5 years`

@export When does my Medicare Part B initial enrollment period begin, if I first become eligible at 65? (s 1395p(d): seven months, from three months before the month I reach 65)
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`When does my Part B initial enrollment period begin` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the first month of the initial enrollment period` (`the month in which age is attained` `my birth date` 65))

@export When does my Medicare Part B initial enrollment period end, if I first become eligible at 65? (s 1395p(d))
GIVEN `my birth date` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`When does my Part B initial enrollment period end` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the last month of the initial enrollment period` (`the month in which age is attained` `my birth date` 65))

@export If I enroll in Medicare Part B in a given month, from which month am I covered? (s 1395q(a), for months from 2023)
GIVEN `how I enroll` IS A `Part B enrollment` @desc One of: enrolled in the initial enrollment period; deemed enrolled; enrolled in a general enrollment period (1 January to 31 March)
      `year I first become eligible` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the month you first become eligible for Part B (the month you reach 65, or your 25th month of disability benefits)
      `month I first become eligible` IS A NUMBER @desc That month (1-12)
      `year I enroll` IS A NUMBER @desc The year you enroll (or are deemed to enroll)
      `month I enroll` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1-12) you enroll (or are deemed to enroll)
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`From which month am I covered by Part B` MEANS
    `the calendar month numbered` (`the first month of Part B coverage` `how I enroll` (`the month number of` `year I first become eligible` `month I first become eligible`) (`the month number of` `year I enroll` `month I enroll`))

@export What is my monthly Medicare Part B premium for a year, with any increase for enrolling late? (s 1395r(a)(3), (b); 2026 premium; the income-related amount is not included)
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year (only 2026 is covered)
      `months I could have been but was not enrolled` IS A NUMBER @desc The months between the end of your initial enrollment period and the end of the enrollment period in which you enrolled (0 if you enrolled in your initial period)
      `of those, months I had employer group coverage from current work` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those months, how many you were covered by an employer group health plan through your own or your spouse's current employment
      `I enrolled in a special period for lost coverage, TRICARE or exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you enrolled in a special enrollment period under s 1395p(i)(4), (l) or (m)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my Part B premium` MEANS
    `the monthly Part B premium` `calendar year`
        (`the full 12-month periods of late enrollment` `months I could have been but was not enrolled` `of those, months I had employer group coverage from current work` `I enrolled in a special period for lost coverage, TRICARE or exceptional circumstances`)

§§ `Appeals and deadlines`

-- Situation: I have a decision from the Social Security Administration that I disagree with.

@export By what date must I ask for a hearing on a Social Security (Title II) or SSI decision? (s 405(b)(1), s 1383(c)(1): within 60 days after I receive notice)
GIVEN `date I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date you received notice of the decision, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I ask for a hearing` MEANS
    `date I received the notice` PLUS 60

@export By what date must I go to court to review the final Social Security decision? (s 405(g): 60 days after the notice is mailed, or any further time allowed)
GIVEN `date the notice was mailed` IS A DATE @desc The date notice of the final decision after your hearing was mailed to you, ISO 8601
      `further days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc Any further days the Commissioner has allowed you (usually 0)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I go to court` MEANS
    `date the notice was mailed` PLUS 60 PLUS `further days allowed`

@export After Social Security tells me I may be eligible for another benefit, by what date must I take steps to apply for it to stay eligible for SSI? (s 1382(e)(2): 30 days)
GIVEN `date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the notice telling you that you are likely eligible for another payment (a pension, Social Security, unemployment benefits)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for the other benefit` MEANS
    `date of the notice` PLUS 30
